course: dictionary
lesson: 5218
title: Jealousy: a normal feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jealousy is the unhappy, angry feeling you get when you want what someone else has. Maybe they have a new bike, or the attention you wanted went to someone else. «Jealousy is wanting what someone else has, or the attention they get.»
explain: Feeling jealous does not make you a bad person. Everyone feels it, even grown-ups. «"Must be nice" said quietly about a friend's holiday is a small bit of jealousy.» The feeling is normal. What you do with it is the important part.
explain: Jealousy becomes a problem when it makes you unkind. «In Kai's class a girl lied about Kai to the teacher out of jealousy.» The feeling led to a lie, and that hurt Kai. You can notice the feeling, talk about it, and think about the good things you already have.
fact: Jealousy means the unhappy, angry feeling of wanting what someone else has.
fact: Jealousy can also mean the fear that someone you love likes another person more than you.
fact: «Jealousy» is a noun, and its plural is «jealousies».
fact: In stories, jealousy often causes trouble, as with Cinderella's stepsisters and Joseph's brothers.
fact: A big perspective can shrink small jealousies: they still matter, but less.
exercise: «Joseph's brothers felt jealousy when their father gave Joseph a richly decorated coat.» What does jealousy mean here? | *The unhappy, angry feeling of wanting what someone else has | A happy feeling of being proud | Being very hungry for food | A fear of the dark
exercise: Maya's best friend got a new bike. Maya feels jealousy. Which is a healthy way to handle it? | Pretend you never feel anything at all | *Talk about it and notice the good things you already have | Tell lies about the bike to the teacher | Take it out on your friend by being unkind
exercise: What is the plural of the noun «jealousy»? | *jealousies | jealouses | jealousyes | jealousys
test: In «In Kai's class a girl lied about Kai to the teacher out of jealousy», what did the jealousy lead to? | A prize for the girl | A new friend for Kai | *A lie about Kai | A party for the whole class
test: Which is a good way to handle jealousy? | *Be happy for others and think about what you already have | Keep it secret and be unkind to others | Take it out on your brother | Pretend the feeling is not there
exam: Which statement about jealousy is true? | Only bad people ever feel it | *Everyone feels it sometimes, and it becomes a problem only if it turns into unkindness | It means feeling proud of someone | It always means you should stop being friends
